ecPath` on the bin via `node:child_process` `spawnSync`, writing fixtures to a temp dir (`fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), ...))`). Check that `node --test` run from `packages/jsonl-lint` discovers these files.\n5. Create `packages/jsonl-lint/README.md` covering what the tool does, usage (`node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <file>`), the output format, exit codes 0/1/2, the `lint(text)` API and how to run the tests.\n6. Update the root `README.md`. The \"What is here\" section currently says there are no tools yet and that `packages/` is empty. Replace that with a bullet that lists `packages/jsonl-lint` (by name, `jsonl-lint`) and gives a one-line description.\n7. Run `npm install` at the repo root so `package-lock.json` picks up the new workspace, and commit the updated lockfile. CI's `npm ci` fails if the lockfile is out of sync. Then run `npm ci && npm test` at the root and make sure the jsonl-lint tests run and all pass. Also run the CLI by hand on a clean file, a file with a bad middle row and a torn last row, a missing path, and with no argument, and check the output and exit codes.\n8. Commit everything, push, and open exactly one PR on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test. The PR body must contain the line `Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102`. Wait for the `test` workflow to finish on the PR head commit and confirm it succeeded. If it fails, fix it and push to the same PR; don't open a second one.","verifier":"Verify the pull request for https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102 at its head commit. Check out the PR head and run every command below from the repository root. First run `npm ci` so the workspace installs from the lockfile. Do one check per acceptance line, in order, and report PASS or FAIL for each with the evidence (the command output).\n\nCheck 1. Expect line: \"packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <file> prints <file>:<line>: <error> for every row that is not valid JSON (1-based lines, blank lines skipped, an unterminated last line checked) and exits 1 if any, 0 if none\"\nRun:\n```\nd=$(mktemp -d); printf '{\"a\":1}\\n\\n[1,2]\\n' > \"$d/clean.jsonl\"; printf '{\"a\":1}\\n{bad\\n\\n{\"b\":2}\\n{\"c\":' > \"$d/bad.jsonl\"; node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js \"$d/clean.jsonl\"; echo \"exit=$?\"; node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js \"$d/bad.jsonl\" 2>&1; echo \"exit=$?\"; echo \"dir=$d\"\n```\nPASS if all of these hold:\n- The clean-file run prints nothing before its `exit=0`.\n- The bad-file run prints exactly two report lines and then `exit=1`. The first starts with `<dir>/bad.jsonl:2: ` and the second with `<dir>/bad.jsonl:5: `, where `<dir>` is the printed `dir=` value. Each line has a non-empty error text after `: `.\n- No line is reported for line 3 (blank) or for lines 1 and 4 (valid JSON).\nFAIL if:\n- any of the above differs, or\n- line 5 (the unterminated last row) is missing, or\n- the line numbers are off (not 1-based, or blank lines not counted in the numbering), or\n- the output format is not `<file>:<line>: <error>`, or\n- either exit code is wrong.\n\nCheck 2. Expect line: \"A missing file or no argument prints to stderr and exits 2\"\nRun:\n```\nnode packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js /nonexistent/missing.jsonl >/tmp/jl-out.txt 2>/tmp/jl-err.txt; echo \"exit=$?\"; echo \"stdout:\"; cat /tmp/jl-out.txt; echo \"stderr:\"; cat /tmp/jl-err.txt; node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js >/tmp/jl-out.txt 2>/tmp/jl-err.txt; echo \"exit=$?\"; echo \"stdout:\"; cat /tmp/jl-out.txt; echo \"stderr:\"; cat /tmp/jl-err.txt\n```\nPASS if both invocations show `exit=2` and some non-empty text under `stderr:`.\nFAIL if either exit code is not 2, or either stderr is empty. An uncaught Node stack trace with exit 1 is a FAIL.\n\nCheck 3. Expect line: \"packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js exports lint(text) returning [{ line, error }]\"\nRun:\n```\nnode --input-type=module -e \"import { lint } from './packages/jsonl-lint